# Fingerprints of verified false positives.
#
# Fingerprint-based, NOT a rules override. An earlier attempt used a
# .gitleaks.toml [[rules]] block with a bare id to allowlist these; that
# REDEFINES the rule with no regex and silently disabled generic-api-key
# repo-wide. The scan then reported clean while a planted AWS key went
# undetected. A gate that passes because it was broken is worse than the
# false positives it was meant to quiet.
#
# Both entries are internal/secretbox/testdata/python_fernet.json, the Fernet
# compatibility fixture:
#   key        a throwaway generated for the test, verified to differ from the
#              production key and referenced by no other file
#   bot_token  the literal string 1234567:AAH-thisLooksLikeATelegramToken --
#              a fake shaped like a real one, which is the point of the case
#
# Each line pins one finding at one commit. A NEW secret in this same file
# gets a different fingerprint and still fails the scan.
